    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d621">

                <pb facs="0681" n="667" xml:id="pg667"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense(M)Peru/64: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-25T11:00:00-04:00">March 25, 1942—11
                            a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>259. Your 284 of March 21. Rubber Reserve informs us that price offered by Rubber
                    Reserve Company for Peruvian rubber is exactly same as price being paid Brazil
                    for same grade. Point can be quickly cleared up when Dasso is here.</p>
                <p>Any question of establishing tire factory in Peru is probably out of question as
                    far as this country is concerned.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
